format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: inside-the-atom

lesson protons-neutrons-electrons
title: Meet the atom
minutes: 4
xp: 50
teaches: u1-particles
teaches: u1-nucleus
relies_on: u1-matter-is-atoms

description:
    Every atom has a tiny centre called the nucleus, with electrons around it. You will meet the three particles of an atom and see which are positive, which are negative and which have no charge.

cite ref-openstax-chem-ch2
supports: The three particles and their charges; the nucleus holds the majority of the atom’s mass.

cite ref-openstax-up3-ch10
supports: The nucleus is an extremely small space at the center of an atom.

cite ref-rutherford-1911
supports: The gold-foil experiment (optional story).

card c04
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Three particles
figure: particle-cards
figure_at: 0

body:
    Every atom is built from just three kinds of particle. [[proton|Protons]] are positive, [[electron|electrons]] are negative, and [[neutron|neutrons]] have no charge, which is how they got their name. Different elements are made from the same three particles, only in different numbers.

card c05
kind: item
type: item
item: u1-l2-match-particles
connected: true

card c06
kind: sim
type: atom-builder
scored: 0
task: Build a helium atom: 2 protons, 2 neutrons and 2 electrons.
hint: Add particles with the plus buttons. Helium has two of each.

config:
    {
      "mode": "build",
      "goal": {
        "protons": 2,
        "neutrons": 2,
        "electrons": 2
      },
      "maxProtons": 6,
      "maxNeutrons": 6,
