    }

card c02
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: A tiny centre
figure: atom-model
figure_args: [2,2,2]
figure_at: 1

body:
    The protons and neutrons are packed together in a tiny centre called the [[nucleus|nucleus]]. The electrons are outside it, and that leaves a lot of room between them. So the nucleus is only a speck, and the atom is mostly empty space.

card c01
kind: item
type: item
item: u1-l2-predict-stadium
scored: 0

card c07
kind: teach
type: reveal
scored: 0
title: The stadium, answered
predicts: c01
figure: stadium-marble
figure_at: 0

body:
    If an atom were a football stadium, its nucleus would be a marble in the middle. The electrons would be far out, and the rest is mostly empty space. The marble is tiny, but it holds the protons and neutrons, so almost all of the atom's mass is packed into it.

