card c11
kind: teach
type: story
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: How do we know?
speaker: npc-hal
tag: Go deeper
figure: gold-foil
caption: Simplified and not to scale.
figure_at: 1

body:
    [[ernest-rutherford|Ernest Rutherford]]'s team fired tiny particles at thin gold foil. Most went straight through, so atoms must be mostly empty. A few bounced straight back, so each atom must have a tiny, heavy centre.

card c12
kind: teach
type: explain
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: Not tiny planets
figure: electron-cloud
figure_at: 1

body:
    Pictures often show electrons on neat rings, like planets. A better picture is an [[electron-cloud|electron cloud]]: the electrons are somewhere in a fuzzy region around the nucleus.
